    "narrative": "With today\u2019s limited slate, **Liam Hicks** stands as our most viable offensive anchor, carrying an efficiency score of 53.01. Batting out of the #3 hole against Armstrong, **Liam Hicks** benefits significantly from a favorable dynamic platoon split (+11%) and a manageable opposing xERA of 4.35. While the park factors at this venue dampen his raw projection slightly, the high-leverage lineup placement outweighs these headwinds. Conversely, **Brayan Rocchio** sits at the lower end of our starting threshold with a score of 43.06. Although **Brayan Rocchio** faces a targetable arm in Peralta, his bottom-of-the-order assignment (-8% adjustment) and the marginal nature of his current production profile make him a player we are monitoring closely to see if a late-inning pinch-hit replacement might offer a higher ceiling for stolen base accumulation.\n\nThe optimization logic currently keeps the bench stagnant due to scheduled off-days for core contributors **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**, all of whom hold scores of 0.0 due to inactivity. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us without our most critical speed-demon for this rotation. Because our depth options\u2014such as **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2014are also inactive today, we are effectively playing with a diminished squad. Given that stolen bases are our most scarce category, the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.** and our elite speed anchors makes today a \"preserve caps\" day rather than an aggressive pursuit of categorical gains. We are essentially riding **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio** through the noise, hoping for a high-traffic game from **Liam Hicks** to stabilize our AVG and RBI categories while navigating the lack of speed options on the active bench.",
